4553</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8302418-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8302418</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new"  format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI STEEL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAGA HISAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKURAYA TOSHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADA CHIKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI STEEL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI, MASATO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAGA, HISAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKURAYA, TOSHIKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, CHIKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAGA HISAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKURAYA TOSHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADA CHIKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAGA, HISAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKURAYA, TOSHIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, CHIKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for treating a stainless steel refining slag which comprises treating a slag generated in a refining process for stainless steel so as for the slag to have a basicity of 1.3 to 4.0 and then mixing the slag in molten state with a substance containing a sulfur having a valency of zero or a negative value in an amount such that the slag has a sulfur content of 0.2 wt % or more. The method can be used for modifying the above slag so that Cr&lt;6+&gt; does not elute from the plug substantially perfectly, which results in the effective use of the slag as a material of a pavement base which is free from the danger of environmental pollution. It is preferred for efficient modification that the cooling of the slag mixed with the sulfur-containing substance from 1200  DEG C to 400  DEG C is carried out rapidly, i.e, within a time of 48 hrs.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé de traitement de scories d'affinage d'acier inoxydable, qui consiste à traiter les scories produites au cours de l'affinage d'acier inoxydable de sorte qu'elles aient une alcalinité comprise entre 1,3 et 4,0, puis à les mélanger en état de fusion à une substance renfermant du soufre de valence nulle ou négative en quantité telle que lesdites scories aient une teneur en soufre de 0,2 % ou plus. Ce procédé peut servir à modifier les scories susmentionnées de manière à ce que Cr&lt;6+&gt; n'élue pratiquement pas de la colonne, ce qui permet d'utiliser ces scories comme base pour revêtement de chaussée ne présentant pas de danger pour l'environnement. Pour que la modification soit efficace, il est préférable que le refroidissement de 1200  DEG C à 400  DEG C - des scories mélangées à la substance renfermant du soufre s'effectue rapidement, soit en l'espace de 48 heures.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>